Mastodon API importer
=====================

This is an importer for microblogging servers exposing the Mastodon API. This
includes Mastodon as well as Pleroma.

It imports the account's own statuses, not its reblogs, as children of the
root's "statuses" node, keyed by their URIs. A status's node, of camliNodeType
"mastodon:status", has its text as written, from the server's
/api/v1/statuses/:id/source (Mastodon 3.5 and later), as its content and
title; its HTML as the server rendered it, as contentHTML, unless that's just
the text's paragraphs and lines; and its visibility, content warning, language,
link preview, and the IDs of the status and account it replies to. Its media are
its children, such as camliPath:image1, of camliNodeType "mastodon:image" (or
"mastodon:video", "mastodon:gifv", "mastodon:audio"), with the file as
camliContent, alt text as description, and a video's preview image as
camliContentImage.

Each page of statuses is stored with a few claims: one of the camliPaths of its
new statuses, and one multi claim of the changes of all its statuses and their
media. An incremental run stops at the first page that's unchanged, and doesn't
fetch the text or media it already has of a status, unless the status has been
edited since. Set PERKEEP_MASTODON_FULL_IMPORT=1 to look at all statuses.

The API's rate limit, by default 300 calls every 5 minutes, is shared with the
account's other apps. A run leaves a fifth of it for them, waiting for the rest
of the window when it's used the rest, so a first run of an account of many
statuses, which fetches each one's text, takes a while: about 240 statuses
every 5 minutes.
